      "content": "1. Tissue – Definition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A tissue is a group of similar cells working together to perform a specific function.",
        "Plant tissues are classified into actively dividing Meristematic Tissues and specialized Permanent Tissues.",
        "Permanent plant tissues are subdivided into Simple (Parenchyma, Collenchyma, Sclerenchyma) and Complex (Xylem, Phloem) tissues.",
        "Animal tissues are categorized into Epithelial, Connective, Muscular, and Nervous tissues based on function.",
        "Xylem transports water and minerals, whereas Phloem conducts synthesized food throughout the plant."
      ],
      "id": "d9jxec4"
