    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Xylem conducts water unidirectionally, while Phloem conducts food bidirectionally.",
        "Sclerenchyma consists of dead cells with lignified walls providing mechanical strength (e.g., coconut husk).",
        "Blood, bone, cartilage, and adipose are all classified under Connective Tissues.",
        "Meristematic tissue cells lack vacuoles and are found in active growth regions like root and shoot tips."
